 but no 600-unit-gap time-respecting chain does.\n\nKey findings:\n- Under the 600-unit constraint, 1006's temporal forward-reachable set is only **8 nodes** and does not include 1860 (step_02), nor any of 1860's four in-neighbours 153/182/958/1390 (steps 08\u201311). Zero enumerated paths (step_12).\n- Ignoring the gap constraint, 1006 *does* reach 1860 \u2014 but the route needs 9 hops with waits of 372, 4961, 217, 2873, 2104, 1930, 1025, 9109 units (step_03): seven of eight inter-hop gaps grossly exceed 600. So ignoring time yields a false positive.\n- Relaxing to 1200 and even 2000 units still fails (steps 17, 13), so the negative is robust, not knife-edge.\n- Confounder controls: the window is busy (7200 events, 1941 active nodes; step_01) and the intermediaries are high-degree hubs (153: 162 events/134 partners; 1680: 72; 182: 68; 45: 61 \u2014 step_14), yet volume/popularity does not produce a valid chain. Both endpoints are themselves sparse (5 events each; step_04) with 1006's single event to 45 (step_15) and activity spread thinly across bins (step_16), leaving no dense temporal corridor.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 and 1860 are connected only when time order and the 600-unit gap limit are ignored. The single time-respecting route requires waits up to 9109 units between hops, and with max_wait=600 the forward-reachable set from 1006 is just 8 nodes, excluding 1860 and all of its in-neighbours. The failure persists at max_wait 1200 and 2000. High-volume hub intermediaries and an otherwise busy window do not create a valid chain, so the apparent link is a static-connectivity artifact rather than a genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 41558, "total_output_tokens": 3931, "total_tokens": 45489, "total_latency_ms": 55852, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}